# Learning Rules

## Auto-Append Trigger

After completing any feature or significant fix, append a concise entry to the relevant `learned/README.md`.

## Entry Format

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — <short title>
**What**: one sentence describing what was done.
**Why**: the reason this approach was chosen over alternatives.
**Gotchas**: anything non-obvious a future agent should know.
```

## Scope

| Work type | Append to |
|-----------|-----------|
| New feature | `.cursor/skills/add-feature-mobile/learned/README.md` |
| Core change | `.cursor/skills/add-feature-mobile/learned/README.md` under a `### Core` sub-heading |
| Deferred / risky change | Mark entry with `[PENDING]` — see `apply-pending` skill |

## Gated Learn for `core/`

Before modifying anything under `lib/core/`, read `learned/README.md` for prior decisions.  
Do not change core abstractions without recording the rationale as a new `learned/` entry.

## Deferred Learnings

If a desired change is too risky to apply immediately, record it with `[PENDING]` at the start of the entry title. The `apply-pending` skill will pick these up later.
